### The .http collection we grow every session.
### VS Code: install "REST Client" and click "Send Request" above any block.
### JetBrains: built in.
###
### S10 starts it with the two probes. Auth lands in S13, tables in S18.

@host = http://localhost:3000
@api = {{host}}/api/v1

### Liveness — must answer 200 even when the database is down.
GET {{host}}/health
Accept: application/json

### The same probe through the /api/v1 prefix the Vite dev proxy forwards.
GET {{api}}/health
Accept: application/json

### Readiness — 200 only while the database is reachable AND migrated.
### Point DATABASE_URL at a file with no schema and this turns 503 while
### /health stays 200. That difference is the whole reason there are two.
GET {{host}}/ready
Accept: application/json

### Readiness through the prefix.
GET {{api}}/ready
Accept: application/json

### A request id you supply comes back on the response and appears in every
### log line for the request — paste one here, then grep the dev console.
GET {{host}}/ready
x-request-id: manual-trace-001
Accept: application/json

### ★ Must be 404. There is no admin surface on the public port (12 §2.4).
### The admin app answers the same path on :3100, which is never published.
GET {{host}}/admin/api/v1/users
Accept: application/json

### Any unknown route: 404 in the standard error shape,
### { "code": "NOT_FOUND", "i18nKey": "errors.notFound" } — never English prose.
GET {{api}}/no-such-route
Accept: application/json
